# NOTE (docs/adr/0016): managed/ is now compiler 0.31.1 output -- the only compiler whose
# runtime (0.16.0) and ledger (8.0.2) the released midnight-js 4.1.1 can deploy. The ZK
# artifacts the BROWSER needs are published separately under public/midnight/ and ARE
# committed, because the deployed site has to serve them for in-browser proving.
# Compiler output. `contract/` (the compiled circuit JS, ~160K, no zkir/key
# dependency -- confirmed by grep) is committed on purpose: src/midnight/circuit.js
# imports it directly for the browser bundle, and Vercel builds from a fresh
# clone with no compile step, so it must exist in git or the build breaks
# (this is exactly what broke the Vercel deploy -- see docs/adr/0012).
# `compiler/`, `keys/` (~28MB of ZK proving/verifying keys), and `zkir/` are
# still generated-only, reproducible with `npm run compile`, not needed by
# anything that imports from managed/ at the JS level.
managed/*/compiler/
managed/*/keys/
managed/*/zkir/

# managed-devnet/ (npm run compile:devnet -- compiler 0.31.1, matched to midnight-js-contracts'
# pinned compact-runtime@0.16.0 per the official compatibility matrix) is only ever used by
# Node scripts that regenerate it on demand -- nothing in it is imported by the browser bundle,
# so unlike managed/ above, the whole thing stays gitignored. Lives inside devnet-deploy/ (not
# directly under contracts/) so Node's module resolution finds THAT package's isolated
# compact-runtime@0.16.0 instead of the top-level 0.19.0 -- see docs/adr/0013.
managed-devnet/
devnet-deploy/midnight-level-db/
